there are two ways to solve for the  square root of a number we can either  use a calculator of course everybody  would love to use this option and the  other way is to solve it manually  manually - we can solve it in two  different ways  one by using the prime factorization  method which we have already seen we  split the number to its prime factors  and then choose one number from each  pair the other method which we will look  at in this video is called the long  division method the name sounds fancy  but don't worry if you follow the steps  given in this video you will never go  wrong but why can't we just use prime  factorization every time well if the  number is large it will take us a lot of  time to reduce it to its prime factors  and the chances of going wrong are very  high  hence prime factorization is useful only  for small numbers and for large numbers  we can use the long division method  let's solve a couple of examples to  understand how the long division method  works look at the number 8281 if we have  to reduce this number to its prime  factors we would first have to think of  all the divisibility rules and so on and  that would take us a lot of time so for  such large numbers we use the long  division method the first thing we need  to do in the long division method is to  draw lines like this a line on top and  align to the left of the number when you  draw a line on top of the number  remember to leave some space above the  number once you're done drawing these  lines you're ready for the first step  the first step is to mark pairs of  digits from the unit's end the unit's  end is the number one so we mark pairs  of digits from right-hand side this  becomes our first pair from the right  the number 81 we continue to mark pairs  till we cover all digits of the number  the next pair will be 82 so the first  step was simple we just mark pairs from  the right which gives us 2 pi  is 82 and 81 now we look at the first  pair from the left which is 82 in the  second step we have to find the perfect  square which is equal to or lower than  82 since 82 is not a perfect square we  choose the perfect square lower than 82  the perfect square just lower than 82 is  81 even 64 is a perfect square  lower than 82 but remember we always  choose the one which is closest we know  that 9 squared equals 81 we just found  out the most crucial number it's the  number 9 9 is basically the square root  of the closest perfect square we write  the number 9 here to the left of the  number this was actually the most  important step of the long division  process to find the first number the  next step is one of the easiest steps  but it's a step where most the students  get confused the step says multiply  above and add below but what do we  multiply and what do we add it is the  same number 9 let's focus on multiplying  above first we multiply 9 with 9 and  write the product here so the 9 you're  multiplying is written on top now let's  come to add below we add 9 with 9 and  write the sum underneath 9 plus 9 gives  us 18 we multiply the same number with  itself  above and wrote the product here and we  added the same number with itself and  wrote the sum here  remember when we multiply or add we're  doing the operation with the same digit  in this case it's 9 so we have completed  three steps first we found the pairs  from the right second we found the  perfect square and wrote a square root  here third we multiplied above and add  it below if you observed it well you  could see that I have left some space  next to the sum of nines that space is  kept for  box so we draw an empty box here and  inside this box we will be writing some  digit our next aim is to find this digit  the next three steps are super simple we  just subtract the product from the  number above it the product we got was  81 the number above it is 82 we subtract  81 from 82 and get 1 and then we get the  next pair down the next pair is 81 so we  write it next to 1 then we draw the same  box above and below above we draw it  next to 9 and below we draw it under the  original box the digits contained in  each of these boxes are the same the  next step according to me is the most  interesting step of the long division  method we use trial and error to find  the digit in the boxes we look for the  product of two numbers which gives us  181 this is how the product should look  what number do you think we can write in  the boxes to get 181 as our product  remember the digits in both the boxes  have to be the same yes 181 multiplied  by 1 gives us 181 so we have found the  digit in the boxes  it's 1 after we find this digit we go  back to the third step and follow the  same procedure multiply above so we  write a 1 and a 1 in these two boxes and  get the product of 181 and one as 181  then we add below we add 1 281 and get  182 then we subtract the product from  the number above it so we subtract 181  from 181 and get a 0 the moment we get a  0 here and there are no more pairs left  we are done  but wait where's the square root of 8281  well it's the number you got on top it's  91 the square root of 8281  is 91 trust  me it's not difficult it's just a little  lengthy let's review what we just did we  marked pairs from the unit's end which  gave us two pairs 82 and 81 then we  choose a perfect square which is equal  to or lower than the leftmost pair 82 we  found out that 81 is the closest square  we write at square root to the left then  we multiply above 9 x 9 equals 81 and  added below 9 plus 9 equals 18 and with  18 we leave space for one more digit  then we reach the three simple steps  first we subtract the product 82 minus  81 gives us 1 second we get the next  pair down and then we draw the same box  above and below which will contain the  same digit as the original box and to  find the digit in the boxes we use trial  and error and get 181 x 1 as 181 so the  number in the box  will be 1 after we find the number in  the box we go back to the third step we  multiply above 180 1 x 1 gives us 181  then we add the same digit below 180 one  plus one equals 182 then we subtract the  product 181 - 180 1 gives us 0 and since  there is no pair left we stop and get  the square root as 91 remember inside  the two lines we always subtract an  outside we always add to get a better  idea see the second part of this video  in which we have solved for the square  root of another number using this same  procedure  you  [Music]  you
 

